            <ArticleTitle>Anomalous origin of the left main coronary artery from the right sinus of Valsalva with coronary AV fistula of the conus artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>203-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 44-year-old man with atypical chest pain, anomalous origin of the left main coronary artery from the right sinus of Valsalva with coronary AV fistula of the conus artery is presented. I am aware of no other report of this combination of anomalies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
